From: RemoteOS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] IPC: serialize unconditional NowPlayingInfo fullscreenMode

NowPlayingInfo stores its MediaPlayerEnums::VideoFullscreenMode field even
when ENABLE(VIDEO) is false. The serialization description still conditionally
omits that field and names MediaPlayer's alias. On i386 the generated layout
check correctly fails (80 versus 84 bytes); 64-bit padding hid the mismatch.

Use the actual always-defined field type and serialize it in all builds.
Retain the type, size and member-order validation checks.

Upstream: Not submitted (appliance compatibility patch)
--- a/Source/WebKit/Shared/WebCoreArgumentCoders.serialization.in
+++ b/Source/WebKit/Shared/WebCoreArgumentCoders.serialization.in
@@ -5598,9 +5598,7 @@ struct WebCore::NowPlayingInfo {
     bool isPlaying;
     bool allowsNowPlayingControlsVisibility;
     bool isVideo;
-#if ENABLE(VIDEO)
-    WebCore::MediaPlayer::VideoFullscreenMode fullscreenMode;
-#endif
+    WebCore::MediaPlayerEnums::VideoFullscreenMode fullscreenMode;
 }
 
 struct WebCore::PlatformMediaCapabilitiesVideoConfiguration {
